    {"step": 1, "tactic": "LDAP user enumeration", "technique": "T1110.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-12-13 10:18:08 UTC on WS-CONTRACTOR-02, AMSI EID 4104 captured a powershell.exe scriptblock invoking DirectorySearcher with filter '(&(objectClass=user)(objectCategory=person)(!(userAccountControl:1.2.840.113556.1.4.803:=2)))' (active users only) on the corp.local naming context. SizeLimit=20 returned a list including alice, bob, j.dupont, m.solano, e.koval, svc_app, svc_sql01, helpdesk, jenkins, ops + others.", "chain_reason": "LDAP enumeration filter (!UAC:0x2) selects only enabled accounts — the precondition step of T1110.003 password spraying. The attacker harvests samAccountNames to use as spray targets."},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Single-password spray via WNetAddConnection2 — 10 accounts in 8 seconds", "technique": "T1110.003", "what_happened": "Between 2033-12-13 10:18:42 and 10:18:50, AMSI EID 4104 captured Add-Type with DllImport for mpr.dll!WNetAddConnection2 + NETRESOURCE struct, then a foreach loop sending 10 IPC$ auth attempts to DC-CORP-01 with password 'Spring2026!' against {alice, bob, j.dupont, m.solano, e.koval, svc_app, svc_sql01, helpdesk, jenkins, ops}. Each attempt 800ms apart. Rule 92310 triggered.", "chain_reason": "10 different users + same single password 'Spring2026!' = textbook password spray (T1110.003). The 800ms inter-attempt delay deliberately keeps each account below the lockout threshold (usually 5 failures in 30 min) while still cycling fast."},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Security 4625 burst on DC + Security 4771 PreAuth-fail burst", "technique": "T1110.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-12-13 10:18:42-10:18:50, DC-CORP-01.corp.local Security log recorded 10 Security 4625 (Account Failed to Log On) events with LogonType=3 (Network), workstationName=WS-CONTRACTOR-02, IpAddress=10.40.55.202, 10 distinct TargetUserName values. AND 8 Security 4771 (Kerberos Pre-Auth Failed) events for those same accounts with status=0x18 (wrong password) from same IP. Rule 18113 + 18114 triggered.", "chain_reason": "10 distinct 4625 events from one source IP in 8 seconds + 4771 PreAuth fail across the same accounts is the mathematically clear password-spray signature. Lockouts didn't trigger because each account got only 1 attempt (below the 5-failure-in-30-min corp policy)."},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "AMSI Invoke-DomainPasswordSpray + tool literals + lockout policy recon", "technique": "T1110.003", "what_happened": "At 2033-12-13 10:18:58, AMSI EID 4104 captured scriptblock literals: 'Invoke-DomainPasswordSpray -Password Spring2026! -OutFile spray.txt', 'kerbrute passwordspray --domain corp.local users.txt Spring2026!', 'crackmapexec smb dc01 -u users.txt -p Spring2026!', 'hydra -L users.txt -p Spring2026! smb://dc01.corp.local', 'rubeus.exe brute /users:users.txt /passwords:passwords.txt'. AMSI also captured 'net.exe accounts /domain' = corp lockout policy recon. Rule 92310 secondary fire.", "chain_reason": "Five named offensive-tool literals in one scriptblock + lockout-policy recon = full T1110.003 toolkit awareness. The attacker checks the corp lockout threshold before spraying to ensure attempts stay below the lockout limit."}
